<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">9 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 9 September, from 9 to 1956.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">9 CE <span class="tih-ago">2,017 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Germanic tribes destroy three Roman legions in the Teutoburg Forest</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Arminius led Germanic warriors in an ambush that wiped out three legions under Varus over several days, by tradition ending around this date. Rome never again tried to conquer Germany beyond the Rhine.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arminius">Arminius</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1087 CE <span class="tih-ago">939 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William the Conqueror dies in Rouen</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">William I died of injuries received at the burning of Mantes. Normandy went to his eldest son Robert and England to William Rufus, a division that set his heirs against each other.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/united-states" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-states.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1776 CE <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Congress adopts the name 'United States of America'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Continental Congress resolved that wherever 'United Colonies' had been used, the new nation should be styled the 'United States'. The name had appeared in the Declaration two months earlier.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1850 CE <span class="tih-ago">176 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">California becomes the 31st US state</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">California entered the Union as a free state under the Compromise of 1850, two years after gold was found at Sutter's Mill. Its admission upset the balance between free and slave states.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1948 CE <span class="tih-ago">78 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">North Korea is proclaimed under Kim Il-sung</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Democratic People's Republic of Korea was proclaimed in the Soviet-occupied north, weeks after the Republic of Korea in the south. Kim Il-sung founded a dynasty that still rules.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1956 CE <span class="tih-ago">70 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Elvis Presley first appears on The Ed Sullivan Show</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Some 60 million Americans, over 80 per cent of the TV audience, watched Elvis's first appearance on Sullivan's show. The 'waist up' camera shots came only on his third appearance in 1957.</p></div></li></ol>
